RF.put("questb:b14",{"8494":{"id":8494,"t":"The Alliance Needs Iron Bars!","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Requires level 1 instead of 40.","obj":"Bring 20 Iron Bars to Corporal Carnes at the Military Ward in Ironforge.\n20 Iron Bar","desc":"Well hello there, Mr./Ms. Fancypants, aren't you a sight for sore eyes. In case you hadn't heard while you were out there \"adventuring\", the Alliance has been gearing up for a war in Ahn'Qiraj and is in need of iron bars... a whole mess of 'em. Bring them to me in stacks of twenty. We can count on you, right, ‹class›?","rew":"You will receive:\n10 Alliance Commendation Signet Ahn'Qiraj War Effort Supplies","back":"If you have those twenty bars of iron, I don't want to know where you have them hidden!","done":"Well, well, if it isn't ‹name›. And you pulled through. I guess now I'll have to keep my eye on you. It hurts me to say this, but thanks for your efforts. The Alliance won't forget, and neither will I. Now get out there and bust your hump on whatever else needs collecting.","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":61.5,"y":31.6,"n":"Corporal Carnes","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ahnqiraj-war"]},"95534":{"id":95534,"t":"Strahnbrad mystery","lv":36,"min":25,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Solve the mystery of Strahnbrad and report your findings in town in Hillsbrad.\nDiscover the fiery mystery of Strahnbrad\nSinged Note","desc":"<The note is singed in places, but is still readable.>\nRumor has it those old bellows have a mind of their own, springing to life when no one is watching. I don't care if it's a ghost story, you'd better get to the bottom of it before I return.\nThere's great power in Strahnbrad, I know it.\n< The rest of the note is singed and torn, as if burnt by fire magic. >","rew":"You will receive:\nBrilliant Cloak\nMoney: 40 0 gold, 40 silver, 0 copper Experience: 2,800\nAlterac Mountains Open the zone on the world map Start an item: Singed Note Level 36 , requires level 25 Difficulty 25 32 34 39 46 Side Both factions Quest ID 95534","cats":["alterac-mountains"]},"1134":{"id":1134,"t":"Pridewings of Stonetalon","lv":21,"min":18,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 12 Pridewing Venom Sacs to Shindrell Swiftfire in Astranaar.\n12 Pridewing Venom Sac Pridewing Patriarch 40 % , Young Pridewing 40 % , Sorrow Wing 40 % , Pridewing Consort 40 % and 2 more","desc":"We are not in open war with the Horde, but our peace is fragile. We often find their agents moving against us, but they do so covertly.\nOne such advance was revealed to us from hidden sources in Theramore, claiming that the orcs collect venom from the pridewings near Mirkfallon Lake, in the Stonetalon Mountains to the south. Orc assassins then use the venom on their secret death raids against the Alliance!\nIf this is true, then we must stop them, ‹name›. We must deny them their source of venom.","rew":"Money: 13 0 gold, 13 silver, 0 copper Experience: 1,650\n+100 reputation with Darnassus","back":"Do you have the pridewing venom sacs, ‹name›? We cannot allow the orcs to use the beasts' poisons against us!","done":"Thank you, ‹name›. It saddens me to order the slaughter of creatures who may not willingly aid our enemies, yet it is my duty to do so.\nYour heart might weep for the pridewings you slew, my friend, but may your heart then swell in knowing that your allies are safe from the pridewings' venom.\nAshenvale Stonetalon Mountains","pins":[{"z":"Ashenvale","x":34.7,"y":48.8,"n":"Shindrell Swiftfire","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ashenvale"]},"1054":{"id":1054,"t":"Culling the Threat","lv":25,"min":18,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring Dal Bloodclaw's Skull to Raene Wolfrunner in Astranaar.\nDal Bloodclaw's Skull Dal Bloodclaw","desc":"Directly to the north of Astranaar are the Thistlefur furbolg. My scouts report that their numbers have grown greatly over the past few months. If they grow too great, they may find the courage to attack Astranaar directly.\nKill as many of their kind as you can, but bring me their chieftain's skull as proof that their efforts have been stifled... for now.\nI shall remain here in Astranaar and await word from you. Elune be with you.","rew":"You will receive:\n2 Restoring Balm\nMoney: 18 0 gold, 18 silver, 0 copper Experience: 2,000\n+100 reputation with Darnassus","back":"The furbolgs' corruption has caused Ashenvale to become a fraction of its former glory.","done":"Well done, ‹name›.\nWe are under constant threat from the furbolg. Hopefully this will keep them at bay for a bit longer.","pins":[{"z":"Ashenvale","x":36.6,"y":49.6,"n":"Raene Wolfrunner","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ashenvale"]},"5534":{"id":5534,"t":"Kim'jael's \"Missing\" Equipment","lv":53,"min":47,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Find Some Rune that the naga have in their possession in the Ruins of Eldarath and return it to Kim'jael in Azshara.\nSome Rune Spitelash Enchantress 8 % , Spitelash Battlemaster 8 % , Spitelash Myrmidon 8 % , Spitelash Siren 8 %","desc":"What?! What?!\nThat wasn't good enough for you? You know how expensive those explosives are? They sell for... oh, nevermind. Fine, you want to make some real money? Cause that's how business is done: you prove you're a valuable employee and then you're rewarded adequately after you stick it out some.\nIf you're a \"valuable\" employee, then hit the Ruins of Eldarath and find me some rune that them Blood elves were lookin' for. The naga apparently have it in their possession.","rew":"Money: 1 60 1 gold, 60 silver, 0 copper Experience: 6,550\n+150 reputation with Booty Bay\n-750 reputation with Bloodsail Buccaneers","back":"Well, ‹name›? Where is the rune? You are a good employee, right? You're here to help?\nDon't make me think twice about paying you what we agreed upon. What? Oh, we didn't agree on anything? Oh, great... then take your time--just know that it'll be a lot less if you take a long time.","done":"Haha! Wonderful!\nI'll be sure to find out what this is for and why Magus Rimtori--she's the cow that hired me--wanted it. Hah! I got you now, stinkin' Blood elves! Kim'jael! Ha! I'll teach them who the rats are!\nYa did good, ‹name›. Thanks a bundle. Here, take this coin and be off with ya--I've got some things to figure out.","pins":[{"z":"Azshara","x":53.5,"y":21.8,"n":"Kim'jael","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["azshara"]},"734":{"id":734,"t":"This Is Going to Be Hard","lv":42,"min":35,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak to Lucien Tosselwrench in the Badlands.","desc":"Wonderful, wonderful.\n<Lotwil looks up at you for a moment before going back to his shackles.>\nGo speak to Lucien, ‹name›. I need a cog #5. Bring it to me, will you?","done":"Cog #5, huh? Yeah, this isn't going to be good.","pins":[{"z":"Badlands","x":25.9,"y":44.9,"n":"Lotwil Veriatus","s":1},{"z":"Badlands","x":25.8,"y":44.2,"n":"Lucien Tosselwrench","e":1}],"cats":["badlands"]},"4734":{"id":4734,"t":"Egg Freezing","lv":60,"min":57,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Use the Eggscilloscope Prototype on an egg in the Rookery.\nEggscilloscope Prototype\nProvided: Eggscilloscope Prototype","desc":"‹name›, I've been working hard on a new device, the eggscilloscope! It's designed to project a burst of cold energy at the egg of a black dragon... and freeze it solid! Can you test it for me?\nI heard that high up in Blackrock Spire, the dragons have a rookery where they hatch their eggs. That's where you'll have to go to test the eggscilloscope, and then let me know how it worked!\nAnd don't worry. Frozen dragon eggs should be harmless. It's the unfrozen ones you have to worry about!","rew":"You will receive:\nEggscilloscope\nMoney: 1 80 1 gold, 80 silver, 0 copper Experience: 8,300\n+150 reputation with Steamwheedle Cartel","back":"‹name›, did you test the eggscilloscope?","done":"It worked? Splendid! I knew it would!\nWhile you were gone I was working on a new version of the eggscilloscope. This one has a much longer range.\nHere, you can have one in case you go back to Blackrock Spire.","pins":[{"z":"Burning Steppes","x":65.2,"y":24,"n":"Tinkee Steamboil","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["blackrock-spire"]},"4974":{"id":4974,"t":"For The Horde!","lv":60,"min":55,"side":"Horde","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 9,950 experience instead of 10,900, 0.91 times as much.","obj":"Travel to Blackrock Spire and slay Warchief Rend Blackhand. Take his head and return to Orgrimmar.\nHead of Rend Blackhand Warchief Rend Blackhand","desc":"Rend dares make such grand claims because of the protection he is afforded by the black flight.\nYou, ‹name›, will find a way to pass through the Halls of Ascension. You will then find 'Warchief' Rend Blackhand and you will destroy him - FOR THE HORDE!\n<Thrall slams a fist down upon his throne.>\nThe next time you return to my chambers, you will hold his head high in triumph and then you shall present it to your Warchief. Do this and be honored as a hero of the Horde.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nMark of Tyranny Eye of the Beast Blackhand's Breadth\nMoney: 2 70 2 gold, 70 silver, 0 copper Experience: 9,950\n+200 reputation with Orgrimmar\n+200 reputation with Darkspear Trolls\n+200 reputation with Undercity\n+200 reputation with Thunder Bluff","back":"<Thrall grunts.>","done":"You have dealt a crippling blow to the forces of Blackrock, ‹name›. With their Warchief slain, the Blackrock legion is once again thrown into the maw of chaos.\nIn honor of your heroics, the people of Kalimdor shall be rewarded!","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":31.7,"y":37.8,"n":"Thrall","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["blackrock-spire"]},"97934":{"id":97934,"t":"Camping 101 leatherworking","lv":6,"min":4,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Speak with Chaw Stronghide in Bloodhoof Village to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.\nRaise your leatherworking skill to 20","desc":"You've become a leatherworker. Good for you, ‹class›. I reckon I know someone that can teach you how to make yourself a tent that will keep you cool on hot days, and dry on rainy days.\nWith a good tent over your head, you'll ensure that you get all the rest you need to stay sharp on your travels.","done":"There you have it, your very own camp tent. Most folk don't care much for tents being set up in the center of town, so you'll need to head into the wilderness if you want to test it out.\nOh, and just remember, no camp is complete without a campfire. You'll need one of those before you start up your camp. Most cooks can teach you to make a fire. If you haven't already, you might want to check in with someone who can train you in the culinary arts to learn the basics.","pins":[{"z":"Mulgore","x":46.2,"y":67.2,"n":"Kaga Wildhoof","s":1},{"z":"Mulgore","x":45.4,"y":57.8,"n":"Chaw Stronghide","e":1}],"cats":["camping"]},"94254":{"id":94254,"t":"Craftsmans writ greater adepts robe","min":1,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever. Its level is not known yet.","obj":"Acquire the items requested by the customer and deliver them to the location marked on your map. This writ must be in your possession to complete the transaction.\nCraftsman's Writ: Greater Adept's Robe\nGreater Adept's Robe","desc":"<Penned in faded ink, the note is requesting $2oa Greater Adept's Robe, along with information about delivery location and payment. At the bottom appears text denoting this writ is transferable.>","back":"<Magus Tirth begins to cast Polymorph: Chicken on you.>","done":"My new robe! Delightful!\nAt long last, I can don my robe AND my wizard hat.","pins":[{"z":"Thousand Needles","x":78.2,"y":75.8,"n":"Magus Tirth","e":1}],"cats":["crafting"]},"94334":{"id":94334,"t":"Craftsmans writ masterwork target dummy","min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever. Its level is not known yet.","obj":"Acquire the items requested by the customer and deliver them to the location marked on your map. This writ must be in your possession to complete the transaction.\nCraftsman's Writ: Masterwork Target Dummy\nMasterwork Target Dummy","desc":"<Penned in faded ink, the note is requesting $2oa Masterwork Target Dummy, along with information about delivery location and payment. At the bottom appears text denoting this writ is transferable.>\nStart an item: Craftsman's Writ: Masterwork Target Dummy Level 0 , requires level 1 Difficulty 1 3 Side Both factions Quest ID 94334","cats":["crafting"]},"7934":{"id":7934,"t":"50 Tickets - Darkmoon Storage Box","lv":60,"min":6,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Item #19182","rew":"You will receive:\nDarkmoon Storage Box","back":"Step right up, step right up! If you have tickets from the Darkmoon Faire you'd like redeemed, then just say so! You can redeem tickets in various denominations for wondrous and fantastic prizes. Don't be shy, give it a try!\nItem #19182 (50)","done":"Here you go, here you go! A prize fit for a king! Congratulations to you, my friend!\nIf you have more tickets you'd like to turn in, then please let me know! For as long as the Darkmoon Faire is here, I'll redeem your tickets.\nMulgore Elwynn Forest","pins":[{"z":"Mulgore","x":38.2,"y":44.7,"n":"Gelvas Grimegate","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":41.5,"y":68.9,"n":"Gelvas Grimegate","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["darkmoon-faire"]},"92814":{"id":92814,"t":"I need a tailor","lv":35,"min":30,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Maintain your reputation with the Gelkis, and bring a White Bandit Mask to Molkar in the Gelkis Village in Desolace.\nWhite Bandit Mask\nGelkis Clan Centaur:","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nPattern: Stormcloth Gloves Pattern: Silk Reagent Bag\nMoney: 18 0 gold, 18 silver, 0 copper Experience: 2,050\n+1,000 reputation with Gelkis Clan Centaur\n0 reputation with Magram Clan Centaur\nLevel 35 , requires level 30 Difficulty 30 31 33 38 44 Side Both factions Quest ID 92814","cats":["desolace"]},"1374":{"id":1374,"t":"Khan Jehn","lv":37,"min":30,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring the Khan Jehn's Head to Uthek the Wise in the Gelkis Village in Desolace.\nKhan Jehn's Head Khan Jehn\nReach 3000 reputation with Gelkis Clan Centaur","desc":"The earth speaks to me, and it says that the Magram grow weak. Now it is time to kill their Khan!\nBring me the head of the Magram Khan, Jehn!","rew":"Experience: 2,850","back":"Show me you are a friend of the Gelkis, ‹name›.","done":"Khan Jehn was strong, but stupid. He thought his own strength was great. He did not see that earth magic is stronger. The Magram centaur will now fall without their leader, and the Gelkis will one day rule!","pins":[{"z":"Desolace","x":36.2,"y":79.2,"n":"Uthek the Wise","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["desolace"]},"1454":{"id":1454,"t":"The Karnitol Shipwreck","lv":39,"min":30,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Find Karnitol's Chest in Desolace.","desc":"My first order of business is for the mage Karnitol--a noble of some sort in Stormwind. Seems his ship was attacked by sea giants while off the coast in the northwest of Desolace. He and his servants tried to bring one of his more valuable chests ashore, but when the sea giants attacked in droves, he chose to abandon it and teleport himself and his servants to safety.\nHe wants us to find the chest and its contents, and return it to him in Stormwind.","rew":"Experience: 3,000\n+100 reputation with Ironforge","done":"You notice the chest does not seem to have any water damage.\nThe second thing you notice is that the top has been forced open, and whatever magical traps were set to safeguard it have long been triggered--this much is obvious from the burn marks around its edges.","pins":[{"z":"Desolace","x":66.2,"y":9.6,"n":"Kreldig Ungor","s":1},{"z":"Desolace","x":36.1,"y":30.5,"n":"Karnitol's Chest","e":1}],"cats":["desolace"]},"95214":{"id":95214,"t":"Stolen blasting powder","lv":10,"min":7,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Recover 16 Stolen Blasting Powder from the troggs east of Gol'Bolar Quarry, then return to Quarrymaster Thesten.\n16 Stolen Blasting Powder","desc":"This keg held enough powder to turn King Magni's throne room into an open air courtyard. We've got to get it back from the troggs before they work out how to ignite it.","back":"I hope you've got good news for me?","done":"That should be all the stolen powder. Thank you, ‹class›.\nPlease accept this reward, and... I'd appreciate if you didn't mention this little incident to anyone.","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":69,"y":54.8,"n":"Quarrymaster Thesten","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["dun-morogh"]},"414":{"id":414,"t":"Stout to Kadrell","lv":10,"min":8,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Take the Cask of Shimmer Stout to Mountaineer Kadrell.\nCask of Shimmer Stout\nProvided: Cask of Shimmer Stout","desc":"I've been drinking more of that Shimmer Stout my brother made - it's great stuff! I want a fellow Mountaineer to try it. His name's Kadrell, and he's usually patrolling the road through Thelsamar in Loch Modan.\nTo get to Thelsamar, go southeast through the tunnel, then turn northeast when the path forks into a road. Follow that road straight into Thelsamar.\nGive Mountaineer Kadrell this cask of Shimmer Stout and see what he thinks!","rew":"Experience: 625\n+75 reputation with Ironforge\n+75 reputation with Gnomeregan Exiles","back":"Greetings, ‹class›, and welcome to Thelsamar!","done":"Now, let me have a taste...\nMagni's Beard! This stuff gets your head turning! And it lightens the limbs, too.\nI feel like I can fly!\nDun Morogh Loch Modan","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":86.3,"y":48.8,"n":"Mountaineer Barleybrew","s":1},{"z":"Loch Modan","x":34.2,"y":47.8,"n":"Mountaineer Kadrell","e":1}],"cats":["dun-morogh"]},"174":{"id":174,"t":"Look To The Stars","lv":25,"min":20,"side":"Alliance","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Renamed from Look To The Stars.","obj":"Viktori Prism'Antras of Darkshire wants you to bring him a bronze tube.\nBronze Tube Arcane Nullifier X-21 2.9 % , Mechanized Guardian 2 % , Mechano-Tank 2 % , XT:4 1.9 % and 4 more","desc":"My Gnomish friend, Cog, has promised to help me build a device which will let me peer towards the stars. A truth exists, beyond magic, that can explain the strange transformation in the forest.\nBring to me a bronze tube made by a skilled engineer. That is the first step, according to Cog's blueprint.","rew":"Experience: 2,000\n+100 reputation with Stormwind","back":"Have you found a skilled engineer to create a bronze tube yet?","done":"This is perfect, ‹name›. The first step is complete!","pins":[{"z":"Duskwood","x":79.8,"y":48,"n":"Viktori Prism'Antras","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["duskwood"]},"254":{"id":254,"t":"Digging Through the Dirt","lv":35,"min":20,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","done":"You dig through the semi-loose dirt over the grave...and find the remains of a coffin.\nWithin the coffin you can feel the vibrating scrapes of clawed fingers and the gnashing of rotted teeth...\nWill you open the coffin and retrieve the Embalmer's heart?","pins":[{"z":"Duskwood","x":28.9,"y":30.8,"n":"Eliza's Grave Dirt","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["duskwood"]},"2974":{"id":2974,"t":"A Grim Discovery","lv":45,"min":38,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 20 Grimtotem Horns to Krueg Skullsplitter in Camp Mojache.\n20 Grimtotem Horn Grimtotem Shaman 80 % , Grimtotem Naturalist 80 % , Grimtotem Raider 80 %","desc":"What!? You came across tauren in the area? You're joking! What did they look like!?\nThe Grimtotem clan! You found some of them? Belgrom, one of our masters, has an interest in their kind... he's even put a bounty on them.\nYou have to go back, ‹class›. Go back and bring me their horns... piles of them if you can. The Grimtotem are not to be trifled with or underestimated. Go back and slay them; let the rivers in Feralas run red with their dark blood.","rew":"Money: 65 0 gold, 65 silver, 0 copper Experience: 3,900\n+100 reputation with Orgrimmar","back":"Take my words seriously, ‹class›, the Grimtotem clan is evil. If you've found their whereabouts, then it's up to you to return and strike the first blow against their clan... before they can come into our own lands and raze our own villages, or pilfer our lands.","done":"These are good horns, ‹class›. Well done. I'll take these from you and be sure to tell Belgrom as soon as we return to Orgrimmar. You've helped me twice now, and for that, you have my mark. Perhaps in the future I can help you! Good luck to you.","pins":[{"z":"Feralas","x":75.9,"y":42.7,"n":"Krueg Skullsplitter","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["feralas"]},"494":{"id":494,"t":"Time To Strike","lv":20,"min":19,"side":"Horde","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 775 experience instead of 625, 1.24 times as much. Read from what the game server sent.","obj":"Travel to Tarren Mill to deliver Deathstalker Lesh's message to High Executor Darthalia.","desc":"Be silent and pay attention, ‹class›.\nI was sent to this position in order to survey the town of Hillsbrad. My mission is one of reconnaissance. It is imperative that you send word to High Executor Darthalia in Tarren Mill at once. Let her know that I, Deathstalker Lesh, send the following message:\n\"The raven's cry from the west doth beckon.\"\nFollow the road to the east and pay close attention to the signs. Now, hurry! Off you go to Tarren Mill, and with urgency I might add!","rew":"Money: 6 0 gold, 6 silver, 0 copper Experience: 775\n+50 reputation with Undercity","done":"The raven's cry from the west doth beckon?\nSuperb news! Hillsbrad is ripe for attack. We can carry out our plan of destruction now. Varimathras will be pleased.","pins":[{"z":"Hillsbrad Foothills","x":20.8,"y":47.4,"n":"Deathstalker Lesh","s":1},{"z":"Hillsbrad Foothills","x":62.3,"y":20.5,"n":"High Executor Darthalia","e":1}],"cats":["hillsbrad-foothills"]},"8654":{"id":8654,"t":"Primestone the Elder","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","rew":"You will receive:\nCoin of Ancestry\n+50 reputation with Horde\n+50 reputation with Alliance","done":"It is good to know the people of this land still pay homage to the olden races. I bid you well, ‹name›, and offer you this token...","pins":[{"z":"Silithus","x":21.1,"y":10.5,"n":"Elder Primestone","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["lunar-festival"]},"9054":{"id":9054,"t":"Cryptstalker Tunic","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Huntsman Leopold at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands will make a Cryptstalker Tunic if you bring him the following: 1 Desecrated Tunic, 25 Wartorn Chain Scraps, 4 Arcanite Bars and 3 Cured Rugged Hides.\nDesecrated Tunic\n25 Wartorn Chain Scrap Stoneskin Gargoyle 14.4 % in Naxxramas , Infectious Ghoul 13.5 % in Naxxramas , Spirit of Naxxramas 13.3 % in Naxxramas , Living Monstrosity 12.5 % in Naxxramas and 4 more\n4 Arcanite Bar\n3 Cured Rugged Hide","desc":"I have discovered a use for the carapace of the crypt fiend. I am able to fashion an extremely light and very deadly set of armor by combining the fragments with some of the desecrated magical armors lost in Naxxramas.\nBring me the items I require and I shall fashion for you a suit of armor the likes of which has never before been seen in our world!","rew":"You will receive:\nCryptstalker Tunic\n+200 reputation with Argent Dawn","back":"You got some missing parts for the quest please go and get them all!","done":"Exellent ‹name› !\n, you got everything just as i asked and now i can make a Cryptstalker Tunic.","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":71.7,"y":48.9,"n":"Huntsman Leopold","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["naxxramas"]},"4494":{"id":4494,"t":"March of the Silithid","lv":53,"min":50,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak to Alchemist Pestlezugg in Gadgetzan.","desc":"It would seem that the silithid's intent, nay - reason for being, is to devour everything in their path that is not of their ecology. Their focus is singular, and it is for this reason they are a grave threat to all life on Azeroth.\nWhat we've seen to date is but the first stages. I suspect that their strength comes from deeper in Kalimdor: Un'Goro Crater. Go to Gadgetzan in the Tanaris desert and speak to Alchemist Pestlezugg. Tell him of my theory; he will surely aid us in fighting the silithid.","rew":"Experience: 525\n+10 reputation with Orgrimmar","done":"Yes, I gathered that Zilzibin sent you to me. Your experience in fighting these beasties is priceless; no one to my knowledge has ever dealt with their kind before. As for Zil's idea that Un'Goro Crater is their heart... perhaps it is. Un'Goro is a mysterious and dangerous jungle to the west of here. Perhaps it is also one step closer to figuring out what the silithid are all about.\nOrgrimmar Tanaris","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":56.3,"y":46.7,"n":"Zilzibin Drumlore","s":1},{"z":"Tanaris","x":50.9,"y":27,"n":"Alchemist Pestlezugg","e":1}],"cats":["orgrimmar"]},"91294":{"id":91294,"t":"Touring the grounds","lv":11,"min":8,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Speak to the residents of Bandarion Keep.\nSpeak with Hilda the Breaker\nSpeak with Jorin Croge\nSpeak with Ander Solliden\nSpeak with Danitha Morr","desc":"Now that the immediate threat of the murloc attacks is under control, I'd encourage you to show yourself around our stronghold. It isn't much yet, but it's home.\nWhen you are done exploring, seek out Danitha Morr, our leader. She can help you get settled in.\nI'm very glad to have met you, ‹name›. May the light be your guide.","rew":"Money: 2 0 gold, 2 silver, 0 copper Experience: 440\n+50 reputation with Undercity","back":"Welcome to Bandarion Keep, ‹class›. It's always good to see a new face.","done":"Breton sent you up here, eh? Excellent.\nMy name is Danitha Morr, and I am the closest thing this keep has to a commander. If you come seeking fellowship amongst those that still remain loyal to the light, you've come to the right place.\nThere's a lot of work to do here before we can fully establish ourselves, and we'd be most appreciative if you would be willing to lend aid.","pins":[{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":21.8,"y":45.2,"n":"Breton Samuels","s":1},{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":22,"y":44.6,"n":"Danitha Morr","e":1}],"cats":["paladin"]},"8414":{"id":8414,"t":"Dispelling Evil","lv":52,"min":50,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Collect 20 Minion's Scourgestones and bring them to High Priest Thel'danis in the Western Plaguelands.\n20 Minion's Scourgestone Skeletal Terror 50 % , Slavering Ghoul 50 % , Hungering Wraith 50 % , Foulmane 50 % and 4 more","desc":"Greetings, ‹class›. Crusaders like you are a welcome sight in these desolate reaches.\nYour holy strength is needed to help fight the endless undead here. We need you to collect a large number of scourgestones and bring them to High Priest Thel'danis. The high priest can be found guarding Uther's Tomb in Sorrow Hill, not far from here.\nOnly one with an Argent Dawn Commission can hope to find scourgestones, so speak to Officer Pureheart if you haven't already.","rew":"Experience: 5,100\n+100 reputation with Argent Dawn","back":"What evil have you brought me?","done":"There is risk in dispelling the evil from a scourgestone, for it attracts the attention of undead for countless miles. But you are strong in the Light, ‹name›, and I do not fear for you...","pins":[{"z":"Western Plaguelands","x":42.7,"y":84,"n":"Commander Ashlam Valorfist","s":1},{"z":"Western Plaguelands","x":52.1,"y":83.3,"n":"High Priest Thel'danis","e":1}],"cats":["paladin"]},"98574":{"id":98574,"t":"Hallowed memorandum","lv":1,"min":1,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Read the Hallowed Memorandum and speak to Branstock Khalder in Anvilmar.\nProvided: Hallowed Memorandum","desc":"While you were helping me out, this memorandum was given to me to pass on to you. Take some time to read it when you have a chance. I'm thinkin' it came from the priest trainer Branstock. Take a gander at it and go find him inside Anvilmar when you've a chance.","back":"Ah, another ‹race› comin' ta learn about the Light! You'll find that deepening your connection to the Light relies on curiosity and intelligence, qualities that many gnomes have in abundance. The way o' the Light isn't a technical discipline, it's a riddle, and one that provides both life lessons and practical blessings.","done":"With time and practice, you'll discover new facets to the Light. In a way, it's finding a union between what you think and what you feel. As you deepen your connection with the Light, you can come back to me to talk about what you've learned. I'll be happy to show you how to tap into that force to teach ya how to heal, or to smite the wicked. For a small donation, of course!","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":29.8,"y":71.2,"n":"Sten Stoutarm","s":1},{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":28.6,"y":66.4,"n":"Branstock Khalder","e":1}],"cats":["priest"]},"8254":{"id":8254,"t":"Cenarion Aid","lv":52,"min":50,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Seek out Ogtinc in Azshara.","desc":"It is the way of the divine to help those in need. The how is insignificant -- only the why matters.\nThe Cenarion Circle has such a need. Speak with Ogtinc to lend aid to their plight. He resides atop the cliffs to the northeast of the Ruins of Eldarath in Azshara.","rew":"Experience: 500","done":"Your arrival has lifted a weight from my shoulders. We have much to do.\nStormwind City Thunder Bluff Darnassus Undercity Dun Morogh Orgrimmar Azshara","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":49.5,"y":44.6,"n":"High Priestess Laurena","s":1},{"z":"Stormwind City","x":49.5,"y":45.2,"n":"Brother Joshua","s":1},{"z":"Thunder Bluff","x":24.6,"y":22.6,"n":"Malakai Cross","s":1},{"z":"Thunder Bluff","x":25.6,"y":20.7,"n":"Father Cobb","s":1},{"z":"Darnassus","x":38.3,"y":81,"n":"Astarii Starseeker","s":1},{"z":"Darnassus","x":37.9,"y":82.7,"n":"Jandria","s":1},{"z":"Darnassus","x":39.5,"y":81.2,"n":"Priestess Alathea","s":1},{"z":"Undercity","x":49.3,"y":17.1,"n":"Aelthalyste","s":1},{"z":"Undercity","x":47.6,"y":18.9,"n":"Father Lazarus","s":1},{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":54.9,"y":22.4,"n":"Theodrus Frostbeard","s":1},{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":55,"y":22.6,"n":"Braenna Flintcrag","s":1},{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":55,"y":22.4,"n":"High Priest Rohan","s":1},{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":36,"y":87.7,"n":"X'yera","s":1},{"z":"Azshara","x":42.4,"y":42.6,"n":"Ogtinc","e":1}],"cats":["priest"]},"94":{"id":94,"t":"A Watchful Eye","lv":21,"min":20,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Take the Glyph of Azora to the Lion Statue near the Tower of Ilgalar in Redridge.\nGlyph of Azora\nProvided: Glyph of Azora","desc":"My rival, Morganth, is a vicious mage of great power who lives in the Tower of Ilgalar in Redridge. I have developed a means of spying on him, the Eye of Azora, and can now view him from afar.\nBut to study his thoughts ... I require further aid.\nIf you are willing, then take my Glyph of Azora to the Tower of Ilgalar. Place it upon the Lion Statue near the Tower.\nWhen this is done, the power of Azora will grant visions of Morganth's future plans.","rew":"Experience: 1,250","back":"This Lion Statue has sat here for decades, and keeps a lonely watch over the infamous Tower of Ilgalar.\nThere is a depression at the base of the statue, where a gem or glyph might be set...","done":"You place the Glyph of Azora on the stone. It adheres itself... and you hear from it Theocritus' disembodied voice:\nYou have my gratitude, young ‹name›. You may now speak with me through this Glyph, and I might have future tasks for you... after I have probed the thoughts of my rival.\nElwynn Forest Redridge Mountains","pins":[{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":65.2,"y":69.7,"n":"Theocritus","s":1},{"z":"Redridge Mountains","x":79.4,"y":46.8,"n":"Old Lion Statue","e":1}],"cats":["redridge-mountains"]},"8814":{"id":8814,"t":"One Commendation Signet","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Alliance Commendation Signet","back":"For those adventurers who have but a single commendation signet, I'll exchange it for a small amount of recognition with the Gnomeregan exiles.\nPlease bear in mind that it is better to hand over a stack of ten signets at once; your efforts will receive greater recognition in doing so. We offer a single signet exchange as a service for those who don't have enough for a full stack of ten.\nWith that being said, I stand ready to assist you if you still wish to hand in a single signet.","done":"Very well - your deeds have been entered into the records, and you are duly recognized for your efforts. Keep up the good work, ‹class›.\nIf you have any more signets to hand in, then I am able to assist you further in that regard.","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":61.2,"y":32.2,"n":"Stormwind Commendation Officer","s":1},{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":62.3,"y":28.5,"n":"Officer Porterhouse","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["reputation"]},"3454":{"id":3454,"t":"The Torch of Retribution","lv":50,"min":40,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Take the Torch of Retribution.","desc":"The torch must now be bound to its owner. Pick up the torch, ‹name›.","rew":"You will receive:\nTorch of Retribution\nExperience: 4,700","done":"You grab the torch with both hands; waves of hatred and anger pulse through your being.","pins":[{"z":"Searing Gorge","x":39.1,"y":39,"n":"Kalaran Windblade","s":1},{"z":"Searing Gorge","x":39.1,"y":39.1,"n":"Torch of Retribution","e":1}],"cats":["searing-gorge"]},"94494":{"id":94494,"t":"Call of water","lv":20,"min":20,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Find Norric Lochthane in Loch Modan.","desc":"Long has it been since ye were last tested, ‹name›. Ye have shown patience thus far in yer studies, but the time has come for ye to learn about the purity of water.\nSeek out Norric Lochthane in Loch Modan. He is along the north western edge o' the lake, south of Stonewrought Dam. Ye will find him there at his burrow hut. Good luck to ye, ‹name›.","done":"The wind's rushin' at yer back, the stone's firm beneath yer boots, and the fire in yer belly's burnin' bright. Aye, it's time ye learned the truth o' water's purity. Yer path's been long, but it's yer spirit that'll carry ye further still. Now, go on, take that first step. The mountain waits for no one.\nIronforge Loch Modan","pins":[{"z":"Ironforge","x":47.4,"y":13.6,"n":"Eldrun Stormbreaker","s":1},{"z":"Loch Modan","x":41.8,"y":19,"n":"Norric Lochthane","e":1}],"cats":["shaman"]},"1534":{"id":1534,"t":"Call of Water","lv":23,"min":20,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Fill the Empty Blue Waterskin at the Ruins of Stardust in Ashenvale and return to Brine in the Barrens.\nFilled Blue Waterskin\nProvided: Empty Blue Waterskin","desc":"Take this waterskin and head deep into the lush forest the night elves call Ashenvale. It is to the far north of the Barrens.\nOnce you've entered the forest, travel west. Along the mountains that separate Stonetalon and Ashenvale, and beyond Lake Mystral, you will find a holy place: the Ruins of Stardust. At the center of the lake you will find a small fountain.\nBring me a sample of the fountain's water. It will be the final component you'll need before I send you back to Islen.","rew":"Experience: 1,400","back":"Do you have the water yet, ‹name›? Tales say the ruins were protected by large creatures of nature that do not care for visitors, but those could be myths to scare off the enemies of the night elves.\nRegardless, be careful.","done":"Wonderful, ‹name›. With all three samples gathered, I can create for you a vial of the purest water any living creature will find. It will be used in the next steps of your rite of passage.\nI am pleased to count you among our kind, ‹name›. You do all ‹class› proud, and I look forward to hearing about your exploits in the future.\nThe Barrens Ashenvale","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":43.4,"y":77.4,"n":"Brine","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["shaman"]},"92894":{"id":92894,"t":"Bone raising","lv":40,"min":35,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Maintain your reputation with the Magram Clan, and use the Enhanced Necromancy Staff to fully raise undead that are struggling to emerge throughout the Valley of Bones. Return to Orgrul once the Magram army has grown.\nSummon or Slay Haggard Bones : 0/ 10\nMagram Clan Centaur","desc":"I can see the excitement in your eyes, outsider. Do you grasp the potential of necromancy yet?\nOf course you do. And that is why I am ordering you to hone your skills further.\nAs you venture deeper into the Valley of Bones, you will see the remains of failed attempts at raising the dead. Gelkis attempts, no doubt. Hardly able to claw out from the dirt. Funny, were it not so pathetic.\nI have imbued your staff with greater power. Use this to grow our army, and crush the ones that fight back!\nLevel 40 , requires level 35 Difficulty 35 36 38 43 51 Side Both factions Quest ID 92894\nThe chain\n14 quests from level 32 to 43, 34,080 XP in all.\n1 [ 35 ] Brutal Politics\nGain a Friendly reputation with the Magram, then speak with Warug.\nCaptain Pentigast Desolace\n2,050 XP\n2 [ 32 ] Assault on the Kolkar\nMaintain your reputation with the Magram.\nWarug Desolace\n2,550 XP\n[ 33 ] Magram Alliance\nGain a Friendly reputation with the Magram, then speak with Warug.\nGurda Wildmane Desolace\n650 XP\n3 [ 33 ] Broken Tears\nMaintain your reputation with the Magram, and bring 3 Broken Tears to Warug in the Magram Village.\nWarug Desolace\n2,650 XP\n4 [ 40 ] A Conqueror's Crown\nMaintain your reputation with the Magram, and return a Conqueror's Crown from the Badlands to Warug in Magram Village.\n3,150 XP\n5 [ 40 ] Valley of Bones\nImprove your reputation with the Magram, and locate Orgrul near the Valley of Bones south of Magram Village.\n320 XP\n6 [ 42 ] Mountain of Bones\nMaintain your reputation with the Magram, and bring 426 Gently Cursed Bones to Orgrul south of the Magram Village in Desolace.\n3,450 XP\n7 [ 42 ] Corrupting Tears\nMaintain your reputation with the Magram, and bring 3 Petrified Bark and 3 Imbued Tears back to Orgrul.\n3,450 XP\n8 [ 41 ] Proof of Concept\nMaintain your reputation with the Magram Clan, then bring 426 Well Cursed Bones from a successful ritual back to Orgrul.\n2,450 XP\n9 [ 40 ] Bone Raising this quest\nMaintain your reputation with the Magram Clan, and use the Enhanced Necromancy Staff to fully raise undead that are struggling to emerge throughout the Valley of Bones.\n2,350 XP\n10 [ 43 ] Bristleback Retreat\nMaintain your reputation with the Magram, and slay quilboar at Bristl","cats":["shendralas"]},"8574":{"id":8574,"t":"Stalwart's Battlegear","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 15 Cenarion Combat Badges, 20 Cenarion Logistics Badges, 17 Cenarion Tactical Badges and 1 Mark of Remulos to Vargus at Cenarion Hold in Silithus. You must also attain Revered reputation with Cenarion Circle to be able to complete this quest.\n15 Cenarion Combat Badge\n20 Cenarion Logistics Badge\n17 Cenarion Tactical Badge\nMark of Remulos\nReach 21000 reputation with Cenarion Circle","desc":"The badges you collect from performing combat, logistics and tactical assignments for Windcaller Proudhorn are more than just for show, ‹name›.\nYou'd be wise to hold on to them. As you prove your loyalty to our organization I can offer you some of the gear we reserve for our closest allies in exchange for those badges.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nDeeprock Bracers Earthcalm Orb Rockfury Bracers Might of Cenarius\nExperience: 3,300\n+50 reputation with Cenarion Circle","back":"It's in our best interest to keep our most loyal allies well geared, ‹name›.","done":"Great work, ‹name›. Please accept this on behalf of the Cenarion Circle. You've certainly earned it, friend!","pins":[{"z":"Silithus","x":51.2,"y":38.9,"n":"Vargus","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["silithus"]},"86574":{"id":86574,"t":"Stonetalon supply run","lv":24,"min":20,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Collect 6 Stonetalon Supplies from Pridewing Wyverns and deliver them to Innkeeper Faralia.\n6 Stonetalon Supply Bundle\nProvided: Stonetalon Supply Satchel","desc":"<The unfortunate body here bears the marks of many strikes from the Pridewing wyverns. The pack nearby is rumpled and discarded, with its contents missing, and only a small note clutched in the courier's hand to indicate what was lost: a shipment meant for Innkeeper Faralia at Stonetalon Peak.>\n<The wyverns have probably carried off the supply bundles to line their nests.>","rew":"You will receive:\nCourier's Wristguards\nMoney: 17 0 gold, 17 silver, 0 copper Experience: 1,950\nStonetalon Mountains Thousand Needles","pins":[{"z":"Stonetalon Mountains","x":48.6,"y":39.8,"n":"Night Elf Courier","s":1},{"z":"Stonetalon Mountains","x":35.6,"y":5.8,"n":"Innkeeper Faralia","e":1}],"cats":["stonetalon-mountains"]},"334":{"id":334,"t":"Package for Thurman","lv":2,"min":1,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Go to the Larson Clothiers in the Stormwind Mage Quarter, and give Thurman Schneider his Sewing Kit.\nThurman's Sewing Kit\nProvided: Thurman's Sewing Kit","desc":"My son Thurman is an apprentice at the Larson Clothiers, in the Mage's Quarter. He was in a hurry today and forgot his shears and needles. I know a great ‹class› like you must have important tasks at hand, but without his tools Thurman can't do his apprentice work!\nPlease, ‹name›. Can you take my son's sewing kit to him? Larson Clothiers is one of two clothing shops in the Mage's Quarter - it's the one deeper in, near the Mage's Tower.","rew":"Experience: 130\n+75 reputation with Stormwind","back":"Are you here to buy clothes?","done":"Oh, blast! I thought forgetting my kit would free me from work. Now I guess I'll have to help the Larsons with their sewing...\nOh, well. Fun will come later I guess.","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":58.1,"y":67.5,"n":"Rema Schneider","s":1},{"z":"Stormwind City","x":52.6,"y":83.4,"n":"Thurman Schneider","e":1}],"cats":["stormwind-city"]},"574":{"id":574,"t":"Special Forces","lv":38,"min":30,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Kill 10 Kurzen Commandoes and 6 Kurzen Headshrinkers.\nReport to Lieutenant Doren at the Rebel Camp.\nKurzen Commando slain : 0/ 10\nKurzen Headshrinker slain : 0/ 6","desc":"Now that many of his regular troops are reduced, you must face his highly trained forces. When they're not in the wilderness slaughtering our rebel soldiers, they are found deep in the back of the Kurzen Compound, in a cave they call the Stockpile.\nI know many of Kurzen's troops personally, and I know they are skilled, loyal, and cruel. This is no easy task I set before you, ‹name›.\nAfter you defeat them, report to Lieutenant Doren, my commanding officer. He will want your report firsthand.","rew":"Experience: 2,850\n+100 reputation with Stormwind","back":"Sergeant Yohwa tells me you are skilled and brave, ‹class›. Do you have something to report?","done":"‹name›. Sergeant Yohwa trusted your abilities, and I trust her. The defeat you brought to Kurzen's forces is almost too much to hope for. I had feared we rebels were alone, and alone we could never stand up against the Colonel's brilliance.\nPerhaps hope of our survival yet remains.","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":38,"y":3.3,"n":"Sergeant Yohwa","s":1},{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":38,"y":3,"n":"Lieutenant Doren","e":1}],"cats":["stranglethorn-vale"]},"5214":{"id":5214,"t":"The Great Fras Siabi","lv":60,"min":55,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 8,300 experience instead of 8,550, 0.97 times as much.","obj":"Find Fras Siabi's smoke shop in Stratholme and recover a box of Siabi's Premium Tobacco. Return to Smokey LaRue when the job is done.\nGrimm's Premium Tobacco Fras Siabi","desc":"Terrible thing... what happened to Fras. You see, the town was sacked and Fras didn't want to leave his precious goods behind. The last thing I remember him saying was, 'I'll burn every last leaf before they get their damned, dirty hands on them!'\nI may love a good stogie but I'm no fool. I left Fras and his delightful store that day. I assume he went down in flames but if there's a chance that even one box of his famous tobacco is still intact...\nWhat do you say, ‹name›? Find a box for ol' Smokey?","rew":"You will receive:\nSmokey's Lighter\nExperience: 8,300","back":"I can't take it, ‹name›! You gotta help me! I'm dying!","done":"Oh sweet, sweet stogie, how I have missed you...","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":70.9,"y":48.4,"n":"Smokey LaRue","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["stratholme"]},"3374":{"id":3374,"t":"The Essence of Eranikus","lv":55,"min":48,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring the Oathstone of Ysera's Dragonflight and the Chained Essence of Eranikus to Itharius in the Swamp of Sorrows. It is there that you will make your choice to aid Ysera's Dragonflight or not.\nItem #10455\nProvided: Oathstone of Ysera's Dragonflight","desc":"You engage the Oathstone, and Itharius speaks directly to your mind through the stone.\n\"By accepting the charge placed in this Oathstone, you agree to aid my cause and the cause of Ysera's Dragonflight in redeeming the corrupted soul of Eranikus. The first sacrifice, one of many you and I will no doubt make, will be to relinquish the gem to me that has chained what free-willed part of Eranikus' psyche remains.\"\n\"Do this ‹name›, and we will work together to redeem a soul worthy of redemption.\"","rew":"Experience: 550","back":"Here we are ‹name›, at yet another crossroads. The time has come to make another choice. What choice do you make, mortal?","done":"You have made your choice, and so it begins. Your choices have been, to date, what I would consider to be the correct ones; your actions and deeds henceforth will determine whether this is to continue.","pins":[{"z":"Swamp of Sorrows","x":13.7,"y":71.7,"n":"Itharius","e":1}],"cats":["swamp-of-sorrows"]},"654":{"id":654,"t":"Tanaris Field Sampling","lv":46,"min":38,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Acquire acceptable samples for 8 basilisks, 8 hyenas, and 8 scorpions. Bring the testing kit back to Chief Engineer Bilgewhizzle in Gadgetzan before the power source runs out.\n8 Acceptable Basilisk Sample\n8 Acceptable Hyena Sample\n8 Acceptable Scorpid Sample\nField Testing Kit sold by Alessandro Luca","desc":"Activating the power source makes the field testing kit start to glow and vibrate. It would seem to be working as planned.\nAccording to Chief Engineer Bilgewhizzle, you now have two hours to collect the data you need in the Tanaris desert. If you do not collect it within two hours, all the data will be lost and you will need to buy another power source from him.\nReturn to him when you have completed the task.","rew":"Experience: 4,050\n+100 reputation with Undercity","back":"Well, did you get everything you needed? If you didn't and the power runs out, everything inside will be ruined and you'll have to start over.\nHey, don't look to me for sympathy; I'm all about the Gadgetzan Water Company making a profit, and if that means selling you power sources until we can afford to import water in from the icy springs of Dun Morogh, so be it!","done":"All right then, it will take me just a second to remove the power source. After that, you can do with it whatever you like now without having to worry about losing the data inside.","pins":[{"z":"Tanaris","x":52.5,"y":28.5,"n":"Chief Engineer Bilgewhizzle","e":1}],"cats":["tanaris"]},"8734":{"id":8734,"t":"Tyrande and Remulos","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Travel to the Moonglade and speak to Keeper Remulos.","desc":"Tyrande will be notifed, mortal. Shan'do Stormrage has prepared me for this contingency.\nNow you must venture to the Moonglade and speak with Remulos. He will have further instruction as to the summoning of Eranikus.\nWe all wish you great luck.","rew":"Experience: 1,650\n+10 reputation with Brood of Nozdormu\n+100 reputation with Cenarion Circle","done":"It would be impossible to pull Eranikus from the Dream should he refuse. His intentions, however, require him to enter our world. He seeks to destroy the living manifestation of Malfurion. To do this successfully would mean an end to one of the most powerful allies of the Dream. The Nightmare would wholly consume all that would remain should Malfurion fall...\nTeldrassil Moonglade","pins":[{"z":"Teldrassil","x":37.6,"y":47.9,"n":"Forest Wisp","s":1},{"z":"Moonglade","x":36.2,"y":41.8,"n":"Keeper Remulos","e":1}],"cats":["teldrassil"]},"894":{"id":894,"t":"Samophlange","lv":14,"min":10,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Access the control console at the Venture Company research site.\nProvided: Control Console Operating Manual","desc":"The Venture Company set up a small research facility far to the north of here, southwest of the Sludge Fen. I don't know very much about what they're doing, but did manage to discover that they're experimenting with something called a \"samophlange\".\nNow what the heck is a samophlange? Well, whatever it is, I want to examine it, so I need someone to go get it.\nI obtained a copy of their control system operating manual, you should be able to figure out how to disengage the samophlange from it.","rew":"Experience: 750\n+75 reputation with Ratchet","done":"A variety of buttons, levers and blinking lights are somewhat erratically arrayed on the face of the control console. A small gauge indicates that the apparatus is currently operating within optimal levels, and indicates that control valves one through three are currently open. There is a small keyhole set into the lower right side of the control panel.","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":63,"y":37.2,"n":"Sputtervalve","s":1},{"z":"The Barrens","x":52.4,"y":11.6,"n":"Control Console","e":1}],"cats":["the-barrens"]},"95774":{"id":95774,"t":"Her name is olgra","lv":20,"min":14,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Slay quilboars and collect 4 of Olgra's Adornments for Mankrik's memorial.\n4 Olgra's Adornments","desc":"The healer who saved me could not save her, and she has died in battle. Her name is Olgra, and I will never forget her.\nYou did not find her adornments on her body? She wore many jewels of polished bone.\nSlay the Razormane Raiders near where she fell, and find her precious works of art!\nI will place them with the memorial that I build in her memory.","rew":"Money: 12 0 gold, 12 silver, 0 copper Experience: 1,550","back":"I have only memories now, but I will build a tribute to Olgra so that they never fade.","done":"I will place these adornments with my wife's memorial, so that I never forget her. My blood will always run hot with revenge!\nYou have done me... done us... a great favor, Johnathon.","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":52,"y":31.6,"n":"Mankrik","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["the-barrens"]},"98094":{"id":98094,"t":"Scout support","lv":25,"min":19,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"High Executor Darthalia wants you to deliver updated orders to Deathstalker Masoj, south of Tarren Mill, outside of Dun Garok\nProvided: Darthalia's Orders","desc":"Now that we can trust you to deliver critical information to our forward spies, there's an extra task for you.\nBring this to Deathstalker Masoj almost directly south of us. He'll have more for you to do once you get there and hand this to him. He is posted on elevated terrain north of the rotten vineyard they call Nethander Stead.\nOur plan to take control of these lands continues steadily.","rew":"Money: 9 0 gold, 9 silver, 0 copper Experience: 2,000\n+150 reputation with Thunder Bluff","pins":[{"z":"Hillsbrad Foothills","x":62.2,"y":20.2,"n":"High Executor Darthalia","s":1},{"z":"Hillsbrad Foothills","x":64,"y":53.8,"n":"Deathstalker Masoj","e":1}],"cats":["the-barrens"]},"99134":{"id":99134,"t":"Discipline","lv":6,"min":4,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Punish 5 Deathguards for Executor Zygand.\nDeathguards motivated (5) Deathguard Linnea Deathguard Abraham Deathguard Phillip Deathguard Lawrence Deathguard Gavin Deathguard Billmuth Deathguard Dillinger Deathguard Randolph Deathguard Saltain Deathguard Mort Deathguard Royann Deathguard Lizabetha Deathguard Simmer Deathguard Oliver Deathguard Bartrand Deathguard Morris Deathguard Lundmark Deathguard Veteran Deathguard Burgess Deathguard Terrence Deathguard Bartholomew Deathguard Cyrus Deathguard Kristof\nDeathguard Linnea\nDeathguard Abraham\nDeathguard Phillip\nDeathguard Lawrence\nDeathguard Gavin\nDeathguard Billmuth\nDeathguard Dillinger\nDeathguard Randolph\nDeathguard Saltain\nDeathguard Mort\nDeathguard Royann\nDeathguard Lizabetha\nDeathguard Simmer\nDeathguard Oliver\nDeathguard Bartrand\nDeathguard Morris\nDeathguard Lundmark\nDeathguard Veteran\nDeathguard Burgess\nDeathguard Terrence\nDeathguard Bartholomew\nDeathguard Cyrus\nDeathguard Kristof","desc":"You are not a member of the Deathguard, and therefore have yet to disappoint me.\nAs a reward for your lack of incompetence, you shall be rewarded with punishing those that have demonstrated such talents in excess.\nSwiftly now--‹name›, is it?--or I shall add your name to my ledger for someone else's reward.","done":"There are precious few delights afforded to us in death. Thankfully, pain is chief among them.\nYou please me this day, and therefore you please the Dark Lady. Perhaps you can be of further use.","pins":[{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":60.6,"y":51.8,"n":"Executor Zygand","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["tirisfal-glades"]},"974":{"id":974,"t":"Finding the Source","lv":55,"min":51,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Krakle in Un'Goro Crater wants you to find the hottest area of Fire Plume Ridge.\nWhenever you find a hot spot, right click the thermometer to check the temperature. Keep looking until you find the hottest one.\nKrakle's Thermometer\nFind the hottest area of Fire Plume Ridge\nProvided: Krakle's Thermometer","desc":"The hot springs here are a source of mystery to me. Where does the heat come from?\nLooking at how close the pools are to Fire Plume Ridge, I really wonder if the volcano might have something to do with it. I created a thermometer to take readings of the temperatures at the volcano, and I'd like to find the hottest part. It gives the measurements in degrees Kraklenheit!\nHere, take it, and take readings of the temperatures at the ridge whenever you see a hot spot!","rew":"Experience: 5,650","back":"I'd go there myself, but... I'm a little scared of the fire elementals there!","done":"Yes, I definitely see the correlation here between the temperature of the volcano and the hot springs. I'll have to double-check my equations for accuracy, but it seems like the distance and the rate that the heat is transferred... Hmm...","pins":[{"z":"Un'Goro Crater","x":30.9,"y":50.4,"n":"Krakle","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ungoro-crater"]},"14":{"id":14,"t":"The People's Militia","lv":17,"min":9,"side":"Alliance","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. New rewards: Boots of the People's Militia.","obj":"Gryan Stoutmantle wants you to kill 15 Defias Highwaymen, 5 Defias Pathstalkers and 5 Defias Knuckledusters then return to him on Sentinel Hill.\nDefias Highwayman slain : 0/ 15\nDefias Pathstalker slain : 0/ 5\nDefias Knuckleduster slain : 0/ 5","desc":"Some Defias have eluded us. My most trusted scout reports that these Defias have been looting and pillaging the countryside, all the way into Southern Westfall. We believe they are hiding out in the Dagger Hills, plotting their next move. Slay the wretches in the name of The People's Militia.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nEdge of the People's Militia Fist of the People's Militia Spark of the People's Militia Boots of the People's Militia\nNew in Forever: Boots of the People's Militia.\nExperience: 1,600\n+150 reputation with Stormwind","back":"‹name›, now is no time for idle chatter. If you still wish to prove yourself to The People's Militia you need to slay the Defias I notified you about earlier. Return to me when you have completed your duty.","done":"When I left the tainted lands of Lordaeron I returned to a grim state of affairs here in my homeland. But there is hope for Westfall yet. As proven by your valor in battle, it is obvious to me that you serve our cause with honor. It is with great pride that I induct thee into The People's Militia. May the Light shine upon you.","pins":[{"z":"Westfall","x":56.3,"y":47.5,"n":"Gryan Stoutmantle","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["westfall"]},"5054":{"id":5054,"t":"Ursius of the Shardtooth","lv":56,"min":53,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Storm Shadowhoof at Everlook in Winterspring wants you to kill Ursius.\nUrsius slain","desc":"In the snowy mountains of Winterspring, to the northwest, a skilled hunter stalks his prey... I speak of Ursius of the shardtooth bears, an agile and clever beast.\nI send you now against him. He roams the sloping hills to the northwest of Everlook. Find and hunt him, before he discovers your intent.\nAll that have gone up against Ursius have quickly found themselves to be the prey, and he, the hunter. Stay on your guard.","rew":"Experience: 5,800\n+100 reputation with Thunder Bluff","back":"Go now, ‹class›. Seek out Ursius.","done":"This was no easy task, yet you have excelled. But do not be too quick to think you have impressed me, ‹name›.","pins":[{"z":"Winterspring","x":61.9,"y":38.4,"n":"Storm Shadowhoof","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["winterspring"]},"94414":{"id":94414,"t":"The anchors of zephras","lv":2,"min":2,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Speak with Halaan Hawk-Eye and borrow his gift to view the anchor pylon in the distance.\nView the Anchor Pylon","desc":"Greetings, young ‹name›. I often times come here to look upon the ancient anchor pylon. Gifts from the spirits of the winds, they bind and sustain our island. Of late however, their magic has grown unstable and inconsistent.\nThey suffer no distress I can see. Their splendor has not changed.\nIf you'd like, I can lend you my gift to look upon them yourself.","back":"My gift is simple, and mundane. I cannot peer between worlds such as those with the skysight, nor can I draw upon the magic of the ley lines beneath Zephras like others can. But a gift it remains and I am grateful to have it.\nAppreciation of what you have is the key to happiness. Yearning for what you may have, or what you have lost, only leads to despair.","done":"Thank you for taking a moment to share this with me. I will continue to watch over the grove, and ponder on the state of our homeland.","pins":[{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":43.8,"y":24,"n":"Halaan Hawk-Eye","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["zephras-isle"]}});